From 3ca764536a7422a32c8af0590205da654b7d68a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:46:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(update): consolidate conflict observations on configured
 integration owner [daveey]

Recurring upstream SHA inventories were copied to independent checkout-local
repair owners because reporting had no explicit integration-owner policy.
Add opt-in update.upstream_conflict_reporting with inventory/pointer modes,
qualified owner and explicit repository/owner-checkout binding. Unset remains
legacy; malformed config or invalid/unreachable owner fails closed.

Inventory only updates the designated existing local owner. Pointers retain
per-checkout incident identity, serialize/dedupe and skip archived/foreign
consumers. Keep the fresh-interpreter reporter and all update custody/pause,
source, acceptance and containment behavior unchanged. No upstream integration.

Proof:
- Behavior RED before routing hookup: 18 failing configured-routing cases.
- Canonical scripts/run_tests.sh: focused routing, stale-module reporter,
  pause ordering, config validation, docs drift and post-swap/update contracts.
- Full scripts/check --base origin/main passed, including health/ruff.
- Prepublication adversarial review corrections: strict malformed-file reads,
  authenticated Board gateway identity, foreign pickup exclusion.
- Website documents atomic config set/get/unset and fail-closed deployment.
